# Live loopback checks for review round 5 G1 (phantom headers) and G2 (non-reading HTTP clients); defensive, local only
# Machine: Apple M2 Pro, 12 cores, 32 GB; macOS 27.2.1. Busy machine (load printed per run); development observations.
# Ports: G1 N1 47311/47312, victim 47321/47322; G2 node 47351/47352, explorer 47353.
# G1 probe: a scratch Rust client over minibtc-p2p's codec (source outside the repo, built in target/probe): each cycle connects from a new port, announces 50 headers with valid PoW on the victim's tip and no blocks behind them, never delivers, reconnects after 25 s. N1 mines a block every 15 s; the victim dialed N1 (outbound). No-retarget devnet params.
# G2: 64 Python clients pipeline requests and never read; one fresh GET /healthz per second until served.

