# Reading: G1 - N1 is never struck (0 stall lines name it) and the victim tracks N1's tip (76 = 76) in both runs; each attacker connection is struck as it stalls (announced=50), and was banned and closed before it reconnected in 9 of 11 cycles (first run) and 8 of 11 (final run). The review measured, before the fix, an honest session struck 8 times and banned at ~180 s with the victim stuck at 60 of 73.
# G2 - RPC: the 1,000-request cap frees a slot within 1 s; explorer: the 10 s write-stall deadline frees slots by 16 s. The review measured lockouts of 45 s (RPC) and 60 s+ (explorer) before, lasting while the clients stayed connected.
